From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add wakelock.h stub for kernels that removed it

The kernel 4.14 for hoki does not export wakelock.h to the staging
headers. Provide a minimal stub that satisfies the prima driver's
includes without requiring the actual wakelock API.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hoki-specific build workaround]

Signed-off-by: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
---
 wakelock_stub/linux/wakelock.h | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wakelock_stub/linux/wakelock.h

diff --git a/wakelock_stub/linux/wakelock.h b/wakelock_stub/linux/wakelock.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1234567
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wakelock_stub/linux/wakelock.h
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: ISC */
+/*
+ * Minimal wakelock.h stub for prima WLAN driver.
+ * The actual wakelock API is not used — prima only includes the header.
+ */
+#ifndef _LINUX_WAKELOCK_H
+#define _LINUX_WAKELOCK_H
+
+#include <linux/ktime.h>
+#include <linux/device.h>
+
+/* wake_lock API removed; prima doesn't actually call these functions */
+
+#endif /* _LINUX_WAKELOCK_H */
--
2.34.1
